  "body": "Found while working #542 (the generic sinker post, `assets/posts/sinker-iso.cps`, \"Sinker EDM (ISO)\").\n\n`assets/machines/AGENTS.md` says the empty wire / sinker templates join the built-in machine library \"with their kind's first post\", because every library machine must have a post (`machine_library`). #542 ships the sinker's first post, but the sinker template still lives only as a test fixture (`crates/app/tests/edm/sinker-edm.mch`). Moving it into `assets/machines/` and `posting::MACHINES` touches the library's own tests and the Setup pane's listing, which were outside #542's scope.\n\nThe template keeps an EMPTY `edm` section (no conditions, no `edm.codes`): posting a burn on it refuses by name for each missing code (#290 D4/D5), which is the intended first experience - the user fills the codes from their control's manual.\n\nDone means: a sinker template `.mch` ships in the machine library, `machine_library` lists \"Sinker EDM (ISO)\" as its post, and a test pins that posting on the unfilled template refuses by name (\"states no edm.codes.<role>\"). Not exercised on a real EDM control.\n\nPart of #290. Depends on #542.\n",
